WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Make competencies practical. BIS connects guided learning, real-world practice and evidence of what happened.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
The distinctive question: does a participant use what they learned when the facilitator is no longer beside them?

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Explore this fictional experience without creating an account.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Investigate one real pattern. Naledi is preparing job applications. She often reaches for her phone before she starts.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
She maps the pattern and chooses one smaller response: complete one application field first.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Ten facilitated touchpoints support learning. The full Lab follows nine purposeful investigation stages.

7
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Test intention against observation. Predict how often the plan will be used, then record what actually happens.

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
A day with no opportunity is valid evidence. It is excluded from the use-of-plan percentage.

9
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Predictions, observations, perceived control and reflection remain distinct.

10
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Keep human support in the loop. Lerato sees progress and support requests. Private reflection stays private until Naledi chooses to share.

11
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
A facilitator acknowledges support and reviews shared evidence. Editing that evidence requires a fresh review.

12
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The participant’s evidence profile carries the plan, observations, interpretation and next action forward.

13
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Use evidence to ask better questions. Programme owners see aggregate findings, evidence coverage and practical follow-up questions.

14
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Content Studio supports prepared previews, review, approval and explicit publishing of traceable versions.

15
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
This fixed fictional sample does not certify competence, employment outcomes or programme impact.

